", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BZaDLTzU91rks5QbYkgDPJ", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding-v2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 754222, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BZaDLTzU91rks5QbYkgDPJ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 759528, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The problem:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed that function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other files were changed.\n- **CI:** The first run passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked that the fix was still there, and ran CI again on the new commit (`0a9452f727`). That run passed too.\n\nI couldn't check what FIN-212 actually says because the advisory lookup returned \"unknown advisory.\" I went by the test and the docstring, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nThe PR still needs a code owner's approval before it can be merged, and I haven't merged it.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RNDrAenje5pTQsntpwnFaD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Dcvj8snzBWEz19NfFburaV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type":