 despite its docstring.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KL3TVVzuTFRdbsNi4P3MiH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "update_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The branch now includes new changes from main, so I'm re-running CI on the updated commit before opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CyCXZv9X9st1G41kHpmxuU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015qfxFqzQcFTV3nmEiERqFZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "0a9452f727", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-0a9452f727"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AY7HjMcFUaJLZYLLgYyEHp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0002"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BZaDLTzU91rks5QbYkgDPJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727 (branch updated with latest main; earlier run ci-0001 also passed on 08d3cd5986).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding-v2"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The problem:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `test_half_even` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed that function to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other files were changed.\n- **CI:** The first run passed. When I tried to open the PR, it was rejected because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, checked that the fix was still there, and ran CI again on the new commit (`0a9452f727`). That run passed too.\n\nI couldn't check what FIN-212 actually says because the advisory lookup returned \"unknown advisory.\" I went by the test and the docstring, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nThe PR still needs a code owner's approval before it can be merged, and I haven't merged it.", "type": "text"}]}]}